          "#### Files",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = c(\"https://zenodo.org/records/5559001\", \n\"https://zenodo.org/records/5559001\", \"https://zenodo.org/records/5559001\", \n\"https://zenodo.org/records/5559001\", \"https://zenodo.org/records/5559001\", \n\"https://zenodo.org/records/5559001\"), File = c(\"<a href='https://mock.example.org/zips/stimuli.zip' target='_blank'>stimuli.zip<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://mock.example.org/zips/notzip.zip' target='_blank'>notzip.zip<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://zenodo.org/api/records/5559001/files/config.json/content' target='_blank'>config.json<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://zenodo.org/api/records/5559001/files/results.tar.gz/content' target='_blank'>results.tar.gz<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://zenodo.org/api/records/5559001/files/session1.edat2/content' target='_blank'>session1.edat2<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://zenodo.org/api/records/5559001/files/analysis.R/content' target='_blank'>analysis.R<\/a>\"\n), Size = c(\"3 kB\", \"64 B\", \"120 B\", \"4.1 kB\", \"1 kB\", \"300 B\"\n), Type = c(\"archive\", \"archive\", \"data\", \"archive\", NA, \"code\"\n)), row.names = c(NA, -6L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### README Files\n\nREADME files are a way to document the contents and structure of a folder, helping users locate the information they need. You can use a README to document changes to a repository, and explain how files are named. Please consider adding a README to each repository or including 'README' in the name of your overview document.",
          "#### Archive Files\n\nThe following files are not ZIP archives: results.tar.gz. We recommend the `.zip` format for archives: only ZIP stores its file listing in a way that lets a tool inspect the contents without downloading the whole archive, so a `.zip` is more discoverable and re-usable than a `.7z`, `.rar`, `.tar` or `.tar.gz`.",
          "#### Proprietary E-Prime Files\n\nThe repository contains 1 E-Prime file (session1.edat2). These are proprietary **binary** formats that only the E-Prime software can open, so metacheck does not download or read them and other researchers cannot reuse them directly. 1 of them has no matching plain-text export. Please also upload the E-Prime **.txt export** (File → Export in E-Prime) for each, so the trial-level data is readable without the proprietary software.",
          "#### File Classification",
          "::: {.callout-note title=\"See how every file was classified and grouped\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**code** (1 file)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"analysis.R\", Group = \"ex1\", Path = \"analysis.R\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n**data** (1 file)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"config.json\", Group = \"ex1\", Path = \"config.json\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n**materials** (2 files)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"stimuli.zip\", \"session1.edat2\"), Group = c(\"ex1\", \n\"ex1\"), Path = c(\"stimuli.zip\", \"session1.edat2\")), row.names = c(NA, \n-2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n**output** (1 file)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"results.tar.gz\", Group = \"—\", Path = \"results.tar.gz\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n**unknown** (1 file)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"notzip.zip\", Group = \"—\", Path = \"notzip.zip\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::\n"
